<Vertical id="wj1_orientations">
<Markdown>
## The Circle's Shorthand: Writer Personalities

The writer's circle developed a list of writer personalities they've noticed talking about writing over
the years.

At the end of the journal, you'll read through the whole deck and **pick the one that sounds most like
you** — and then, as Richard puts it, *say what makes you sure. That's the useful part.*

There are **eight writer personalities**, though the writing circle is always adding more. At the end of
today's journal, you'll browse and choose from them, but there is also an option to **create your own.**
If you want a refresher at any time, click the **Writer Personalities** tab at the top of your screen.

| | Writer personality | In a nutshell |
|---|---|---|
| 🤝 | **Community Writer** *(Alma)* | Writes to connect with people — *"Almost everything I write is pointed at another person."* |
| 🧭 | **Explorer** *(Lee)* | Writes to find out what they think — *"I write to find out what I think about things."* |
| 🔧 | **Technician** *(Richard)* | Writes to get things done clearly and correctly — *"I write so things get done properly the first time."* |
| 🌿 | **Hobbyist** | Writes for the enjoyment of it |
| 💭 | **Dreamer** | Writes to bring imagined stories and ideas to life |
| 🔁 | **Practitioner** | Writes steadily, as a practical habit |
| 🏁 | **Finisher** | Writes to finish something real |
| 🎯 | **Pragmatist** | Writes to reach and affect an audience |
</Markdown>
<Done id="wj1_orientations_done" label="Mark as read" />
</Vertical> <!-- wj1_orientations -->


