<Vertical id="wj1_alma_board">
<Markdown>
## Alma's Writer Board

*"It's just everything you write, laid out. Here — it's faster if I show you mine."*

| Alma writes… | For school / outside | How often |
|---|---|---|
| Texting | Outside | Every day |
| The roommate group chat | Outside | Every day |
| Texts to her family — the aunts get Spanish, the cousins get both | Outside | Every day |
| Emails (professors, work) | For school | A couple times a week |
| Discussion posts | For school | Weekly *("and I resent every one")* |
| Captions when she posts something | Outside | A few times a week |
| Comments on shared docs (group projects) | Both | Adds up fast |
| Study-group notes — she's the one who types them up | For school | Most weeks |
| The planner and the to-do lists | Both | Constantly |
| Shift-swap messages for work | Outside | A few times a month |
| The whole inside of birthday cards | Outside | Every friend, every year |
| Reviews, when a place is actually good | Outside | Now and then |

> *Alma stops partway down.* **"Huh. I always forget how much ends up on here."**
>
> *"The first time I did this I put down three things — essays, emails, texting. I thought that was the
> list. Now it doesn't fit on one screen."*

On her writer board, Alma just listed what she actually writes, and the **volume** surprised her — and
some of it (the group chat, the captions) she wouldn't have called "writing" at all. **That's what you're
about to do next.**
</Markdown>
<Done id="wj1_alma_board_done" label="Mark as read" />
</Vertical> <!-- wj1_alma_board -->


<!-- ===================================================================
     TASK 1 — BUILD YOUR WRITER BOARD  (GENUINE DRAG-AND-DROP)
     Two drag-and-drop boards = the doc's two drop zones (For school /
     Outside school). Within each board the student drags the kinds of
     writing into order, most often (top) -> rarely or never (bottom):
     that ordering is how the doc's per-item "frequency" is captured.
     Each board is a TabularMCQ radio grid (Frequently / Sometimes / Never).
     The board asks only WHAT and HOW OFTEN — never WHY.
     =================================================================== -->

<Vertical id="wj1_board">
<Markdown>
## Your Writer Board

Your turn. This is just an **inventory** of the writing you actually do — it doesn't have to be complete
or tidy, and it isn't asking *why* yet. Just be honest about **what** you write and **how often.**

Your board has **two sides**: the writing you do **for school**, and the writing you do **outside
school.** For each kind of writing, mark whether you do it **Frequently, Sometimes, or Never** — on each
side.

- The same kind of writing can be different on the two sides — that's normal.
- And **count the stuff you don't think counts.** Group chats, captions, lists — Alma almost left those
  off, and they turned out to be most of her board.
</Markdown>

<Markdown>### 🏫 Writing I do **FOR SCHOOL**</Markdown>
<Markdown>*How often do you do each of these **for school**?*</Markdown>
<TabularMCQ id="wj1_board_school">
cols: Frequently, Sometimes, Never
rows:
  - 💬 Texting and DMs
  - 👥 Group chat messages
  - ✉️ Emails
  - 📝 Class notes
  - 🗂️ Lists, planners, and reminders
  - 📱 Social posts, captions, and comments
  - 📄 Essays, papers, and reports
  - 🎨 Creative writing (stories, poems, song lyrics)
</TabularMCQ>
<Markdown>**Anything else you write for school** that isn't a row above? Add it here.</Markdown>
<TextArea id="wj1_board_school_other" rows="3" placeholder="e.g. lab reports, messages in another language, prompts to AI tools..." />

<Markdown>### 🌙 Writing I do **OUTSIDE SCHOOL**</Markdown>
<Markdown>*How often do you do each of these **outside school**?*</Markdown>
<TabularMCQ id="wj1_board_outside">
cols: Frequently, Sometimes, Never
rows:
  - 💬 Texting and DMs
  - 👥 Group chat messages
  - ✉️ Emails
  - 📝 Notes to myself
  - 🗂️ Lists, planners, and reminders
  - 📱 Social posts, captions, and comments
  - 📄 Longer writing (blogs, fan fiction, reviews)
  - 🎨 Creative writing (stories, poems, song lyrics)
</TabularMCQ>
<Markdown>**Anything else you write outside school** that isn't a row above? Add it here.</Markdown>
<TextArea id="wj1_board_outside_other" rows="3" placeholder="e.g. messages to family, texts in another language, journaling, gaming chat..." />
</Vertical> <!-- wj1_board -->


