<Vertical id="wj1_board_noticing">
<Markdown>
## One Thing You Noticed

*Alma leans over:* **"Did anything end up on there that you wouldn't have called writing before you sat
down?"**

You don't have to answer — but if something jumped out, name it.
</Markdown>
<TextArea id="wj1_board_noticing_text" rows="2" placeholder="The thing I almost didn't count as writing was..." />
</Vertical>


<!-- ===================================================================
     TASK 2 — WHY I WRITE
     The board is a list of WHAT. This task adds the WHY. The student checks
     EVERY reason that applies (fixed list + open option) for each cluster of
     their writing, names up to four reasons that come up most, and writes a
     short reflection.

     CheckboxInputs, not dropdowns: people write the same thing for several
     reasons at once, so one reason per kind of writing is the wrong model,
     and each stored value is a LIST of codes. The ideal input would grow on
     demand ("add another reason"); lo-blocks has no repeatable-input block,
     so the fixed checkbox list is the interim shape (bugs.md).
     =================================================================== -->

<Vertical id="wj1_why">
<Markdown>
## Why I Write

Here's the thing a board can't tell you. Two people can write the exact same grocery list — one to get
the shopping done, one because it quiets a busy mind. Same item, completely different activity. *It only
looks the same from outside.*

So go back through your writing and put the **why** on it. For each group below, **check every reason
that's true for you** — as many as fit. There's no right answer.
</Markdown>

<Collapsible id="wj1_why_board_reminder" title="Remind me what's on my board">
<Markdown>*Here's the board you built — most often at the top. You can even nudge it here if you left something out.*</Markdown>
<Markdown>**🏫 For school:**</Markdown>
<Use ref="wj1_board_school" />
<Markdown>**🌙 Outside school:**</Markdown>
<Use ref="wj1_board_outside" />
</Collapsible>

<Markdown>### 💬 Messaging &amp; staying in touch *(texts, DMs, group chats)*</Markdown>
<Markdown>*Check every reason that's true for you — I do this writing…*</Markdown>
<CheckboxInput id="wj1_why_messaging">
  <Key value="dont_do"       > I don't really do this sort of writing    </Key>
  <Key value="stay_in_touch" > To stay in touch with people I care about </Key>
  <Key value="community"     > To be part of a group or community        </Key>
  <Key value="figure_out"    > To figure out what I think                </Key>
  <Key value="try_out"       > To try something out and see what happens </Key>
  <Key value="get_done"      > To get something done or stay organized   </Key>
  <Key value="remember"      > To remember something                     </Key>
  <Key value="proud"         > To make something I'm proud of            </Key>
  <Key value="enjoy"         > Because I enjoy it                        </Key>
  <Key value="feelings"      > To work out how I'm feeling               </Key>
  <Key value="persuade"      > To persuade someone or make a point       </Key>
  <Key value="required"      > Because a class or a job requires it      </Key>
  <Key value="something_else"> Something else (I'll describe it below)   </Key>
</CheckboxInput>
<!-- The "Something else" box for each group is gated on that group's own
       checkboxes, so it opens right where the student made the choice. Every
       option carries an explicit <Key value="…">, so the condition matches
       the stored CODE and survives copy edits to the prose. -->
<Vertical id="wj1_why_messaging_other_box" when="'something_else' in @wj1_why_messaging.value">
<Markdown>*Describe it in your own words:*</Markdown>
<TextArea id="wj1_why_messaging_other" rows="2" placeholder="Mostly, I do this writing to..." />
</Vertical>

